WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.020
- Let's get to it though.

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.090
I just love a great show
and great music, y'all.

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:03.923
Let's get to it, though.

00:00:03.923 --> 00:00:05.190
It's Oscar season.

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.950
So, that time of year
when studios are releasing

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.480
their most groundbreaking movies,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.134
a powerful new film named "Monica"

00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:13.320
is getting a lot of Oscar Buzz.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.120
And, next year could
actually make history,

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.230
which is super cool.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.350
It deals with issues of
dementia and aging parents.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.720
It also stars Patricia
Clarkson, no relation,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.240
but I love her, and Trace Lysette,

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.310
who could be the first transgender woman

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.320
nominated for Best Actress,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.557
and my audience got a chance to see it!

00:00:30.557 --> 00:00:32.074
(audience cheers)

00:00:32.074 --> 00:00:34.272
What did y'all think? Did you like it?

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:35.272
You like it?

00:00:36.645 --> 00:00:37.814
All right.

00:00:37.814 --> 00:00:40.200
And, well, and since it's
Transgender Awareness Week,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.370
we thought it's the perfect time

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.860
to talk about this incredible
film with its stars.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.620
Everybody, please give a
warm welcome to Trace Lysette

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.453
and Patricia Clarkson!

00:00:47.453 --> 00:00:49.760
(audience cheers)

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.927
(upbeat light rock instrumentals)

00:01:12.724 --> 00:01:14.730
We were like "You wore your jeans, yes."

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.470
It's a jeans day.
- It's a jeans day.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.224
I love it.
- I was running late.

00:01:18.224 --> 00:01:19.830
I love.
- I'm just,

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.510
I'm kind of like hooker mom.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.833
- I have no. (laughs)

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.237
Oh my God, we have to be related!

00:01:27.237 --> 00:01:28.745
- No, I wish Kelly.
- Oh gosh.

00:01:28.745 --> 00:01:31.020
- Kelly, I have to tell you,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.470
I so would love to lie,
and say I'm related.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.813
You are so divine.
- [Kelly] I would too!

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.114
- Beautiful, extraordinary.
- Oh!

00:01:39.114 --> 00:01:40.846
- [Patricia] Oh, you're so extraordinary.

00:01:40.846 --> 00:01:41.685
- Ditto!

00:01:41.685 --> 00:01:43.920
- But wait, if you heard me sing one note,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.560
you would know immediately.
I am not related.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.240
- But anyway, yeah. We are not related.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.550
But, I think that we are,
I'm gonna call us sisters.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:51.560
- My mother wishes we could claim you.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.774
- [Kelly] Okay.
- She says.

00:01:52.774 --> 00:01:54.608
You can claim me. I love
you. You're so gifted.

00:01:54.608 --> 00:01:57.000
Well, did y'all meet
before filming "Monica?"

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.868
Did you know each other?

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.465
- No, we didn't.
- No, we met at a party at.

00:02:00.465 --> 00:02:02.460
- An Emmy party!
- Yeah, that's right.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.130
- But, we had both been cast.
- Okay. Very bosh.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:08.183
- And, I saw her across the
crowded room, and I thought,

00:02:08.183 --> 00:02:09.016
"Oh my God,

00:02:09.016 --> 00:02:10.778
she's the most beautiful
woman in this whole room.

00:02:10.778 --> 00:02:11.914
And, I'm her mother!

00:02:11.914 --> 00:02:13.594
(everyone laughs)

00:02:13.594 --> 00:02:15.270
- And, now you're we're sisters.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.615
You're just gaining family members.

00:02:16.615 --> 00:02:17.940
- But, yes, yes.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.850
I play everybody's mother,
beautiful mother, sister. Yes.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.020
I mean, I wanna be everybody's
mother or sister, yeah.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:25.479
- Yeah, but we all are
connected. I do believe that.

00:02:25.479 --> 00:02:28.170
But, "Monica" is pretty personal for you.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.670
This film is pretty personal, right?

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.333
- Oh, yeah. I mean, every
trans story is personal for me.

00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:35.295
"Monica." I mean, there's
so many Monicas out there.

00:02:35.295 --> 00:02:40.295
I feel like our journey with our families,

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.170
and just where we fall in the world,

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:45.180
and how the world makes space for us,

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.860
or doesn't make space for us,

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.929
is always gonna be a fight
that we're gonna have to fight,

00:02:49.929 --> 00:02:52.009
at least in my lifetime, probably.

00:02:52.009 --> 00:02:56.070
But, this movie, it, you
know, it's for the girls,

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.780
it's for the dolls, it's
for the femme queens.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.603
It's for the trans women.
(audience cheers)

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.430
I have been waiting for so long

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.720
for their stories to be told.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.510
It centers on her. It's not
centered on someone else.

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.814
It's through her lens,
which is very different.

00:03:12.814 --> 00:03:16.500
Usually, you know, if there's
a trans person involved

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.650
in a movie, they're not the protagonist.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.953
They're not the centerpiece.

00:03:20.953 --> 00:03:23.070
So, that's why this film is so special.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.950
- But, that's why I said
yes, faster to this film

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:28.687
than any film I've ever
done in my very long career.

00:03:28.687 --> 00:03:30.270
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:33.810
- Because, it was, it kind of
still very emotional for me.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.853
It was not lost on me, Kelly,

00:03:36.803 --> 00:03:39.957
that it would give an
extraordinary transgender actress

00:03:39.957 --> 00:03:43.409
the lead. I said, "I'll be
your backup singer any day."

00:03:43.409 --> 00:03:46.140
I knew how important this film was.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:46.973
- Yeah.

00:03:46.973 --> 00:03:49.230
Tell everybody, like, give,
like, a, kind of a synopsis.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.919
What's the plot for everyone?

00:03:50.919 --> 00:03:54.210
- So, Monica has been
living life on her own

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:59.210
for 20 years or so, and her
mother is in her last days,

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:03.393
and she makes a decision to go home.

00:04:04.535 --> 00:04:07.172
and see what it's giving,
you know. (laughs)

00:04:07.172 --> 00:04:09.240
and see, you know, see what.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.800
- There's so much with
the tone of "giving."

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.727
That was awesome.
- Yeah.

00:04:12.727 --> 00:04:14.062
And, see what it's,

00:04:14.062 --> 00:04:15.600
see what's happening back
where, you know, her roots,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.762
and see if there's a connection
there with the family,

00:04:18.762 --> 00:04:19.595
or, I don't know.

00:04:19.595 --> 00:04:22.170
I mean, her mother's
struggling with memory loss,

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:24.180
and, and brain surgery.
- Brain Cancer.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.144
- Brain cancer.

00:04:25.144 --> 00:04:27.273
- I mean, I'm in my last month.

00:04:27.273 --> 00:04:28.950
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.202
- And, I don't know who she is.

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:31.035
- Right.

00:04:31.035 --> 00:04:32.937
Because she's transitioned,
and I think she's hospice.

00:04:32.937 --> 00:04:37.937
And so, I'm not happy
that this woman is here,

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:42.190
and it's a pas de deux,
of a mother and a daughter

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:47.190
coming to terms with their lives.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.750
But it.
- which is relatable for many.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:49.583
- [Patricia] Yes.
- Oh yes! Oh yeah.

00:04:49.583 --> 00:04:51.240
- Oh, it is about family.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.130
I mean, it's ultimately about forgiveness,

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.529
and love, and hope.

00:04:54.529 --> 00:04:56.760
- [Kelly] Every Family experiences that.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:01.760
- It's about, it is, it's
about unconditional love,

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.250
a mother learning to love
a child unconditionally,

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.250
and a child spending the rest of her life

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.080
with the love of her mother.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:10.913
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:10.913 --> 00:05:13.560
- I've had several people come
up to me that were not trans,

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:18.390
that have just dealt with death,

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:20.947
and caring for their loved
ones in their last days,

00:05:20.947 --> 00:05:23.567
particularly their parents.

00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:25.500
Had an adoptee come up to me

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:27.840
who reconnected with their
birth parent later in life,

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.060
and they were all so moved by this story.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.549
So, there's definitely
a universal theme there,

00:05:32.549 --> 00:05:34.666
beyond the trans of it all.
- Oh, definitely.

00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:35.603
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:35.603 --> 00:05:38.310
- I mean, it will take you far.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:39.540
It, really, and, you know,

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.813
your Josh Close plays our,
you know, my beautiful son,

00:05:43.657 --> 00:05:44.747
your brother, you know,

00:05:44.747 --> 00:05:45.990
it's just got these great, great actors.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:49.269
Adriana Barraza, great,
great, great Mexican actress.

00:05:49.269 --> 00:05:52.549
It's just, it's filled with
really beautiful performances.

00:05:52.549 --> 00:05:54.949
And, it's shot on real film, too.

00:05:54.949 --> 00:05:56.153
- Yeah, that was cool.

00:05:56.153 --> 00:05:58.560
- In such a, yeah.
- I've never looked worse.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.379
She of course, has never looked better.

00:06:00.379 --> 00:06:02.197
(all laugh)

00:06:02.197 --> 00:06:03.593
- Sometimes I'm against high-def.

00:06:03.593 --> 00:06:05.064
- Yeah, right?

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:08.744
- Yeah, I'm like, "you're too
close. You can see it all!"

00:06:08.744 --> 00:06:10.085
(audience cheers)

00:06:10.085 --> 00:06:11.030
We're celebrating Transgender
Awareness Week this week,

00:06:12.629 --> 00:06:14.010
and we're honored to
have these two women here

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.440
to talk about their
acclaimed movie, "Monica."

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.490
So, I have to talk about this.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:19.170
Is it, was it the Venice Film Festival

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:21.480
that y'all got an 11
minute standing ovation?

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.496
- 11 and a half.
- Oh my gosh!

00:06:23.496 --> 00:06:25.586
Because, that's a long time.

00:06:25.586 --> 00:06:27.869
Like, think about it.

00:06:27.869 --> 00:06:30.570
If we sat here for 11 minutes.
(Patricia laughs)

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.130
Yeah. It would be uncomfortable.

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:33.690
- If you applauded us for 11 and a half.

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:35.073
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:06:35.073 --> 00:06:37.002
- Well, it would make our lives, but yes.

00:06:37.002 --> 00:06:37.835
(audience laughs)

00:06:37.835 --> 00:06:39.660
I mean, but she was the
first transgender actress

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:40.890
to ever lead a film,

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:43.130
in the history of the
Venice Film Festival.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:45.742
(audience cheers)

00:06:45.742 --> 00:06:47.026
- Love this, yeah.

00:06:47.026 --> 00:06:50.094
What have you seen from people
that have seen the film?

00:06:50.094 --> 00:06:52.230
Like, what have you seen
as the reaction from, like,

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:53.580
the trans community?

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:54.480
- Oh my goodness.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:58.890
I get, like, long letters on social media,

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.264
just from all over the world.

00:07:01.264 --> 00:07:03.000
Trans people writing me,

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.480
telling me, "Oh my God, it's
the first time I saw myself

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.550
in a movie, you know."
- Represented, yeah.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:11.010
- Right. It's just so much bigger.

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:12.960
It's just, (sighs)

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.490
there's so much at stake for us right now.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:16.431
There's been bills introduced this year,

00:07:16.431 --> 00:07:17.264
like legislation,

00:07:17.264 --> 00:07:19.732
that are just trying to
make our lives harder.

00:07:19.732 --> 00:07:22.182
- [Kelly] Go backwards.
- Erase us all together.

00:07:22.182 --> 00:07:24.780
So, something like this, I don't know,

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:27.247
the visibility brings,

00:07:27.247 --> 00:07:30.780
hopefully brings humanity to our lives.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:33.466
Hopefully, you know, if someone
doesn't know a trans person

00:07:33.466 --> 00:07:34.891
in their own day-to-day lives,

00:07:34.891 --> 00:07:36.813
maybe they can watch a movie like this

00:07:36.813 --> 00:07:39.424
and see Monica's heart,
and see her mother's heart,

00:07:39.424 --> 00:07:44.424
and see that we're deserving
of love, and see the talent,

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:50.030
and, you know, everything that
we can bring to this world,

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.133
and to this industry.

00:07:52.133 --> 00:07:54.180
And, yeah, I mean, it's
been really moving.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.749
So, I think the message
that I get from all over,

00:07:56.749 --> 00:07:59.940
that's what really keeps me going,

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.657
- Look, timing is so divine, right?

00:08:01.657 --> 00:08:04.830
Like, it's what a perfect time
to have something like this

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:05.730
for people to watch.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:07.300
Like, even if you aren't
affected, like you said,

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:09.780
directly impacted in your everyday life,

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.060
to see what is happening
outside of your circle

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.500
is so important.
- Oh yeah.

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:16.440
- It's just important for
us to progress as humans,

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:17.430
like in that sense.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.199
But, our next guest is an icon,

00:08:19.199 --> 00:08:21.221
and it's an honor to have her here today.

00:08:21.221 --> 00:08:22.614
So, let's bring her out now.

00:08:22.614 --> 00:08:25.380
Her podcast is called
"The Laverne Cox Show."

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.870
It's available wherever
you get your podcast.

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:29.733
Everybody, please welcome Laverne Cox!

00:08:29.733 --> 00:08:33.302
(audience cheers)

00:08:33.302 --> 00:08:37.469
(upbeat light rock instrumentals)

00:08:53.068 --> 00:08:54.681
Y'all wanna scooch
down, and we'll come in.

00:08:54.681 --> 00:08:58.442
Well, you look fabulous!
- Thank you.

00:08:58.442 --> 00:09:00.540
- Y'all got the "wear black" memo,

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.559
and we got the "wear
jeans" memo. I like this.

00:09:02.559 --> 00:09:04.438
So, you got to see "Monica."

00:09:04.438 --> 00:09:06.390
So, what are your thoughts?
- Oh my God, yes!

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:07.223
- Yeah.

00:09:07.223 --> 00:09:09.780
- Oh, I love this film so much,

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:13.650
and I just wanted to take a
moment, and take a breath,

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:17.010
because what I love about being an artist,

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:21.787
and being an actor is that,
I think art at its best

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.611
reaffirms what it means
to be human for us.

00:09:25.611 --> 00:09:30.611
A beautiful film, a song,
reaffirms for us as human beings,

00:09:32.752 --> 00:09:34.980
as viewers, what it means to be human,

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:37.770
and helps us to understand
our experiences,

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:41.520
and our lives better, and maybe
to work through something.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.010
And, I think "Monica" operates

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:46.737
at that highest of levels of art,

00:09:46.737 --> 00:09:49.740
where I watched it,

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:53.384
and I understood something
about being human,

00:09:53.384 --> 00:09:55.560
about alienation.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.350
I think that the way the film is shot,

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:01.110
and the way we linger with Monica,

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:05.670
we understand that there's
this distance between her,

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:07.890
and how the world sees her,

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.620
her wanting to make a connection,

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:14.280
but it just keeps falling apart
with the world around her.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:16.470
And, then with the person who should,

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.322
she should be closest to the
most, there's this distance,

00:10:19.322 --> 00:10:22.079
and we, and they don't
see us, and can't see us.

00:10:22.079 --> 00:10:26.857
And, all of us want to just
be deeply seen and known.

00:10:26.857 --> 00:10:28.830
- [Kelly] Everyone.
- Everyone wants that.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.750
And, I think that's what
this movie is about.

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:33.562
And, it illustrates it and
tells a story visually,

00:10:33.562 --> 00:10:35.899
and through these incredible performances,

00:10:35.899 --> 00:10:40.140
in such a way where I feel
like it's a sacred space,

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:42.210
what that is created in this film

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:47.210
of understanding the complicated
relationship of alienation,

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:50.190
distance, longing to be seen and known,

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:54.122
and then the hope, the glimpse of.

00:10:54.122 --> 00:10:55.823
- End of the tunnel, in a way.
- Recognition.

00:10:55.823 --> 00:10:57.119
- Yeah.
- Of recognition,

00:10:57.119 --> 00:10:58.320
of seeing, of understanding.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.574
I wept.
- That's why I took,

00:11:00.574 --> 00:11:01.463
one of the reasons I took the film,

00:11:02.401 --> 00:11:03.598
because I think that's what it is,

00:11:03.598 --> 00:11:04.950
is it is about unconditional love.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:06.390
It's about all of us.
- [Laverne] Yeah.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.333
- Finding unconditional love.
(audience applauds)

00:11:09.333 --> 00:11:11.413
- And, everyone's searching
for it, everybody wants that.

00:11:11.413 --> 00:11:15.720
So, with anti LGBTQ laws
being passed in many states,

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:18.030
what do y'all hope this movie does

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.920
for the awareness of trans people?

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:24.360
- Well, for me, what I
am aware of is that what,

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:27.960
the way that these laws have
been passed is that they've,

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:29.082
it's been a really,

00:11:29.082 --> 00:11:31.920
anti-trans folks have
done a really good job

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:33.210
of dehumanizing us.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.054
They have reduced us to transitions,

00:11:35.054 --> 00:11:35.974
and body parts, and it,

00:11:35.974 --> 00:11:40.080
they've done a really good job
of making us less than human.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:41.580
And, when you can dehumanize people,

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:42.690
you can take away their rights,

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.310
you can commit violence against them.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:48.780
What "Monica" does is deeply
humanizes a trans woman

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:50.160
at the center of a story.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:51.088
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:11:51.088 --> 00:11:52.547
- We are human beings deserving of love,

00:11:52.547 --> 00:11:55.061
deserving of rights and respect.

00:11:55.061 --> 00:11:57.528
And, it's really about
a rehumanizing process

00:11:57.528 --> 00:12:00.147
that has to happen in
relationship to trans people.

00:12:00.147 --> 00:12:03.300
And, great storytelling is
a beautiful way to do that.

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:05.331
- [Kelly] Yeah.
(audience cheers)

00:12:05.331 --> 00:12:06.963
My goodness, you're good.

00:12:06.963 --> 00:12:09.255
- But, I just, I said this before,

00:12:09.255 --> 00:12:11.970
what I don't understand in our country,

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:13.530
we have a great country

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:15.884
when we really live up
to the real values of it.

00:12:15.884 --> 00:12:17.645
- Amen.

00:12:17.645 --> 00:12:21.344
- People cross rivers and
mountains, and they cross oceans.

00:12:21.344 --> 00:12:26.280
They risk their children's
lives to come to this country,

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.320
to flee persecution.

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:31.898
Why do we turn around
and persecute our own?

00:12:31.898 --> 00:12:34.731
(audience cheers)

00:12:35.766 --> 00:12:38.160
- What's your hope, you
know, playing "Monica," like,

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:40.230
what's your hope? What
do you hope this does?

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:43.980
- I mean, well, of course, you
know, I hope it humanizes us,

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:46.530
but I also hope it, I hope
that it opens doors for,

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:49.710
for more stories so
that, because, you know,

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:50.543
we're not a monolith.

00:12:50.543 --> 00:12:53.970
There's so many trans
stories that need to be told,

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:58.970
and we kind of, we need to
knock on that glass ceiling.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:02.040
We need to open up space.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:06.266
And, it's really hard for a
film like this to get funding.

00:13:06.266 --> 00:13:08.790
And so, I know that
whatever comes after this

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:12.000
is gonna have their work cut out for them.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.917
But, if this film does well,
maybe it'll be a little easier

00:13:14.917 --> 00:13:17.130
for whoever comes next.

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:19.740
- And, can I add to that,
for all the folks out there

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:22.290
who are allies, thank you
for doing this show, Kelly.

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:23.123
- Yeah!

00:13:23.123 --> 00:13:24.780
This is the action, this is the work.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:25.774
The people who say that they're allies.

00:13:25.774 --> 00:13:27.000
- That was gonna be my question.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.052
What do you advise people do?

00:13:29.052 --> 00:13:32.058
- The people who stay their
allies and who stand with us.

00:13:32.058 --> 00:13:33.317
- Let's talk about it.

00:13:33.317 --> 00:13:35.064
- Need to put their money
where their mouths are.

00:13:35.064 --> 00:13:36.503
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- That they need to elevate.

00:13:37.712 --> 00:13:39.838
(Trace snaps fingers)
(audience applauds)

00:13:39.838 --> 00:13:42.911
They need to elevate our
stories, fund trans projects.

00:13:42.911 --> 00:13:45.039
I, you know, I'm so
blessed in my work, but I,

00:13:45.039 --> 00:13:45.872
and I just did shot a show.

00:13:45.872 --> 00:13:48.480
It is really hard to get a
trans show, by a trans creator,

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.314
with a trans lead, made,
a TV show, a movie.

00:13:51.314 --> 00:13:53.190
It's all nearly impossible.

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:54.952
And, with all the backlash now.

00:13:54.952 --> 00:13:56.132
- [Kelly] Not unhelpful, yeah.

00:13:56.132 --> 00:13:57.150
- It's even more difficult, right?

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:59.439
With everything that
happened with targeting.

00:13:59.439 --> 00:14:02.550
But, like, earlier this year,
corporations are afraid.

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:04.110
Right? They're scared.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.540
And, if you say you were with us,

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:09.930
now is the time to really show up,

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:13.011
and put your money where
your mouth is, fund projects,

00:14:13.011 --> 00:14:17.827
support us, fight against
this anti-LGBTQ+ legislation,

00:14:17.827 --> 00:14:22.140
and lift up the real lived
experiences of trans people

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:25.230
and actual trans people,
and bring us to the table.

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:28.371
- Absolutely!
(all clap)

00:14:28.371 --> 00:14:30.090
Well, hopefully this is progression.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.280
Like, hopefully people watching
this, people are affected.

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:34.821
They go home, they tell
their family members,

00:14:34.821 --> 00:14:36.984
they tell their friends, and
hopefully that's what happens.

00:14:36.984 --> 00:14:38.850
And, people actually
showing up, like you said.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:39.683
- Yeah.

00:14:39.683 --> 00:14:41.848
Well, Billy Porter was on the
show recently. I love him.

00:14:41.848 --> 00:14:44.520
And, he said this about
dealing with the backlash

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:46.751
against the LGBTQ+ community.

00:14:46.751 --> 00:14:49.107
- What we have to do,

00:14:49.107 --> 00:14:52.230
who are the people in the
positions to make the change,

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:55.560
is understand that the
change has already happened.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:58.030
That's why the pushback is so severe.

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:59.124
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:14:59.124 --> 00:15:01.534
Like, what are your
thoughts on that statement?

00:15:01.534 --> 00:15:03.449
(audience cheers)

00:15:03.449 --> 00:15:05.580
That's, it's exactly right.

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:08.677
A few years ago, I was a vigil for,

00:15:08.677 --> 00:15:12.180
there was a lot of trans
women had been murdered

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.893
in a short span of time.

00:15:14.734 --> 00:15:16.550
And, I was at a vigil in Los Angeles,

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:17.550
and I said,

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:18.383
"It's the best of times,
and the worst of times."

00:15:18.383 --> 00:15:22.528
At that moment, we could go
to, there was a film with,

00:15:22.528 --> 00:15:24.240
starring trans people, "Port Authority,"

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:26.460
that was at the Cannes Film Festival.

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:28.680
Lena Blooms on the cover
of Sports Illustrated.

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.990
Trans people were everywhere
in terms of visibility,

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:33.120
and we're being murdered
disproportionately.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:36.030
And, there are all these anti-LGBTQ+ laws.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.680
Our beautiful visibility,

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:40.800
the beautiful lights that
trans people have inside of us

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:41.647
are shining brightly,

00:15:41.647 --> 00:15:43.590
and people are getting more opportunities

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:44.760
when we're more visible.

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:47.336
And, because of that visibility,
the backlashes happen.

00:15:47.336 --> 00:15:49.217
People are afraid or scared.

00:15:49.217 --> 00:15:51.180
And so, these laws are happening,

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:52.680
and this propaganda is happening.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:55.560
And so, I think we just have to understand

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:56.393
that's what's happening,

00:15:56.393 --> 00:15:59.310
understand that there's a
dehumanizing process going on,

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:01.176
understand that we're being propagandized,

00:16:01.176 --> 00:16:04.530
and then come with love.

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:06.430
Come with love and humanity to each other.

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:07.263
- Open heart.

00:16:07.263 --> 00:16:09.090
- And, understand with open hearts,

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:12.030
understand that this beautiful
light should be shining

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:15.369
and that, it all has to
be about love, you know?

00:16:15.369 --> 00:16:16.202
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:16:16.202 --> 00:16:18.960
- Because, they think the
fear, the fear that people are,

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:20.940
they're using fear, and people are afraid.

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:23.550
And we, a lot of people
don't understand trans folks,

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:27.060
or, you know, we don't know
a trans person personally,

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:28.993
but we're all human.

00:16:28.993 --> 00:16:33.905
And, when we proceed with love,
love, then I think we can,

00:16:33.905 --> 00:16:36.030
as corny as that is.
- Things will fall into place.

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:39.150
- I believe that in my whole
spirit, as corn as it is,

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:42.720
if we can proceed with
love first, and empathy,

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:43.804
It's all good. It's all good.

00:16:43.804 --> 00:16:46.660
(audience cheers)

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:49.050
- Be sure to check out the
movie, "Monica." It's On Demand.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:49.950
Please support it.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:52.050
And, you can also find
"The Laverne Cox Show,"

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:53.643
wherever you get your podcast.

